  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be the points on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math>. Let the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> divide the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> be a directrix of the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and the corresponding focus be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>. If from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, the perpendicular on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, then the length of the latus rectum of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> is equal to",
